  "content": {
    "title": "Tax Day food deals 2026: Free Krispy Kreme, Wendy's and more discounts",
    "text": "To offset the stress of Tax Day, several restaurant chains are offering deals and discounts on Wednesday, April 15, 2026.Joe Raedle/Getty ImagesTax Day is upon us, but don’t stress — several restaurant chains are offering discounts and freebies to make meals easy.Whether you’ve already filed your taxes and are waiting on your tax refund, or need to file a tax extension, these deals are available to all. Whether you’re craving Krispy Kreme doughnuts or a Potbelly sandwich, there’s bound to be a discount to satisfy you.Article continues below this adGet Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.Get Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.ONLY 25¢Here are some food deals you can find in Texas to celebrate the end of tax season on Wednesday, April 15.Krispy Kreme: BOGO dozensOn Wednesday only, customers who buy any dozen doughnuts can get an Original Glazed dozen free. The offer is available in-store, via drive-thru and through the Krispy Kreme app.Article continues below this adPizza Hut: $10 large pizzasPizza Hut is offering large three-topping pizzas starting at $10. Customers can choose from Hand Tossed, Tavern Style or Thin ’N Crispy crusts. The deal is available in-store, online and through the Pizza Hut app.Popeyes: Discounted mealCustomers who order through the Popeyes app or website can get 25% off a three-piece tender combo, which includes tenders, a regular side, a biscuit and a drink.Article continues below this adLoyalty members who spend $10 or more can also get a free item, including a chicken sandwich, two-piece chicken, tenders, fried pickles or wings.Potbelly: BOGO sandwiches/wrapsOn Wednesday only, customers can get a free Original-size sandwich or wrap with the purchase of a Big or Original sandwich or wrap using promo code BOGO.Article continues below this adQdoba: Discounted entrées for 'Guac Relief' surveyQdoba Rewards members can get $5 off a full-size entrée by completing a short survey. The coupon will load April 20 and can be used through April 26.On April 15, Qdoba invites Rewards Members to “file” for Tax Day Guac Relief™ and receive a $5 Reward to use toward any full-sized entrée purchase.Courtesy/QDOBA Restaurant CorporationSmoothie King: $3 off for joining loyalty programCustomers who join Smoothie King’s Healthy Rewards program and download the app on April 15 will receive a $3-off coupon.Article continues below this adSubway: BOGO footlongs, 1040 'refunds'Sub Club members can buy one footlong and get one free through April 28 using promo code FLBOGO.Subway is offering 1,040 randomly selected Sub Club members who use the promo code \"FLBOGO\" on Tax Day, April 15, a surprise free Footlong coupon.Courtesy/Subway RestaurantsOn Tax Day only, 1,040 customers who use the code will receive a surprise coupon for a free footlong, effectively making both sandwiches free.Article continues below this adWendy's: Free nuggets with purchaseCustomers who spend $5 or more on the Wendy’s app can get a free six-piece nuggets on Wednesday.— USA TODAY contributed to this report.Article continues below this adGet alerted to the most important stories and stay on top of the news.April 15, 2026Alexis Simmerman has been a trending reporter for the Austin American-Statesman since January 2024. She is a 2023 graduate of the Missouri School of Journalism and has a Bachelor of Arts in English from the University of Missouri.",
